{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 43, :comments ["<b>Rejoice, O nations, etc.</b> Meaning: when HaShem takes vengeance upon the enemies of Israel and exalts the rank of Israel, the nations will sing over His people Israel to praise and exalt them, as it says (Psalms 144:15): ״אַשְׁרֵי הָעָם״ etc." "<b>For the blood of His servants He will avenge.</b> And His saying ״כִּי דַם etc. and vengeance״ etc. — meaning: not blood alone, but also His enemies who plotted evil against Him, HaShem will repay them with the vengeance they plotted to carry out, in the manner of what He said (Psalms 7:17): ״יָשׁוּב עֲמָלוֹ בְרֹאשׁוֹ״." "<b>And He will atone His land, His people.</b> And His saying ״וְכִפֶּר אַדְמָתוֹ עַמּוֹ״ is the conclusion of the matter He began to say: ״כִּי יָדִין ה׳ עַמּוֹ״ etc., and He concludes by saying that whatever sins still remain upon Israel, the land which had been desolate and a reproach for many years will atone for them — this will serve as atonement for the iniquity of the people of HaShem."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:21:43.752024828Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}